MID_EV13_027_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_027_m01_001: Mmmph...
MID_EV13_027_m01_002: Rrrr... Aaagh...
MID_EV13_027_m01_003: Aaah!
MID_EV13_027_m01_004: Haaah... Haaah...
MID_EV13_027_m01_005: <NCA>Remember your dream.
MID_EV13_027_m01_006: What was that I saw? It was hazy, but...
MID_EV13_027_m01_007: I thought I was in a city of unfamiliar buildings,\nand...I transformed into a dragon.
MID_EV13_027_m01_008: I crushed underfoot all who tried to flee, burning\nthem to ash...
MID_EV13_027_m01_009: And it all felt so real. It seems impossible that this\nwas any normal dream.
MID_EV13_027_m01_010: Could it have been a memory? One belonging to\nsomeone else, perhaps.
MID_EV13_027_m01_011: But if so, whose? What does it mean for me?
MID_EV13_027_m01_012: Am I doomed to be a monster, just like him?
MID_EV13_027_m01_013: That brute Bahr Vahn...
MID_EV13_027_m01_014: He was inhuman from the start, but the man I met\nin the arena seemed almost a demon.
MID_EV13_027_m01_015: It was three years past that he escaped us at the\nshrine of Mahadu.
MID_EV13_027_m01_016: They called this arm one of Drake's treasures. Will its\npower also cost me my humanity?
MID_EV13_027_m01_017: What was that scream?!
MID_EV13_027_m01_018: Your Majesty, we have a trespasser. The guards\nare holding him at bay even now.
MID_EV13_027_m01_019: Think he came looking for something, boss. Maybe\nrevenge on you.
MID_EV13_027_m01_020: To me, all of you! We go to repel the invader!
MID_EV13_027_m01_021: Rrgh... Rrgh...
MID_EV13_027_m01_022: Bahr Vahn! So it was you!
MID_EV13_027_m01_023: You do me a favor by putting yourself in my grasp.\nI will settle our grudge here and now!
MID_EV13_028_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_028_m01_001: This is not over, Queen of Saramis. Next time, you\nwill return that arm to me.
MID_EV13_028_m01_002: You think that you will leave here alive?\nYou murdered my father!
MID_EV13_028_m01_003: Hmph.
MID_EV13_028_m01_004: His strength, as ever, is diabolical.
MID_EV13_028_m01_005: You said it. No human could run on walls and leap\nfences like that.
MID_EV13_028_m01_006: Ah, what's the use. He's too quick for me to hit\nat this distance.
MID_EV13_028_m01_007: If even Lilian can't mark him, he's far beyond any\nordinary man.
MID_EV13_028_m01_008: I want every able soldier in pursuit at once!\nDo not let him escape!
MID_EV13_028_m01_009: Damn it. It's like he disappeared... Where'd he go?
MID_EV13_028_m01_010: Maybe the compass— No, too many of Drake's\ntreasures around to get a clear reading.
MID_EV13_028_m01_011: It'd be impossible to know if it's reacting to him\nor something else.
MID_EV13_028_m01_012: Talimun?! Why are you here?
MID_EV13_028_m01_013: I could ask you the same. I was after Bahr Vahn,\nbut I lost the trail. Have you seen him?
MID_EV13_028_m01_014: <NCA>Answer him.
MID_EV13_028_m01_015: <NCB>Question him.
MID_EV13_028_m01_016: <ACA>We confronted him when he came to attack me as\nI slept.
MID_EV13_028_m01_017: <ACA>I nearly landed a killing blow, but he escaped.
MID_EV13_028_m01_018: <ACB>What is your interest in him?
MID_EV13_028_m01_019: I was in the middle of a little business deal.
MID_EV13_028_m01_020: There's this sword called the Demon Sword\nFragarach—one of Drake's treasures, you see.
MID_EV13_028_m01_021: I got in touch with the owner, a swordsman named\nEsprin, and we were in the midst of negotiations.
MID_EV13_028_m01_022: Just as we were about to close the deal, that hooligan\nBahr Vahn swooped in.
MID_EV13_028_m01_023: He killed poor Esprin and took off with the sword.
MID_EV13_028_m01_024: I went after him, naturally. Almost caught him too.
MID_EV13_028_m01_025: But now... Feels like a good time to be anywhere\nother than Dagsion.
MID_EV13_028_m01_026: Why is that? Has your lack of scruples made you\nan enemy or two?
MID_EV13_028_m01_027: My life has enough complications. I'd rather avoid\nadding to the pile.
MID_EV13_028_m01_028: Rest assured, I'll be back for the next match.\nHopefully things calm down in the meantime.
MID_EV13_028_m01_029: Oh, and Your Queenliness? Keep an eye out for\nOrder of Mithras devilry while I'm away, would you?
MID_EV13_028_m01_030: The Order of Mithras... A mysterious cabal known\nby some as the dark side of Dagda.
MID_EV13_028_m01_031: <NCA>Ask for details.
MID_EV13_028_m01_032: <NCB>Ask their connection to Bahr Vahn.
MID_EV13_028_m01_033: <ACA>I would hear more.
MID_EV13_028_m01_034: <ACA>They are a secret society of alchemists, founded as\na research organization under Dagda the Great.
MID_EV13_028_m01_035: <ACA>They enjoy many special privileges. They have ties to\nthe temples, but few know their true nature.
MID_EV13_028_m01_036: <ACB>Judging by Talimun's warning, I take it they are\ntied somehow to Bahr Vahn.
MID_EV13_028_m01_037: <ACB>They are an enigmatic bunch. They may be working\nwith our adversary toward some hidden motive.
MID_EV13_028_m01_038: Haah.
MID_EV13_028_m01_039: That is enough for tonight. Call off the search, and\nbid the sentries rest.
MID_EV13_028_m01_040: As you wish. But are you certain?
MID_EV13_028_m01_041: I do not take Talimun's warning lightly. Something\nseems awry in Dagda.
MID_EV13_028_m01_042: But the worst thing I could do is let my worry\nconsume me. Besides...he desires my arm.
MID_EV13_028_m01_043: We need not pursue him. He will come to us.\nLook to the sky.
MID_EV13_028_m01_044: What a lovely full moon.
MID_EV13_028_m01_045: When he attacks again, it will be by the light of\na full moon like this one.
MID_EV13_028_m01_046: That is the way of the Har Hali. Our best course is\nto wait for it.
MID_EV13_029_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_029_m01_001: I am told you are Hong Hua, a priest of\nDagda's temple.
MID_EV13_029_m01_002: Are you aware of the serial killings plaguing\nDagsion recently?
MID_EV13_029_m01_003: <NCA>Answer her.
MID_EV13_029_m01_004: <NCB>Question her.
MID_EV13_029_m01_005: <ACA>Yes. They say that skilled warriors are being slain\none after another.
MID_EV13_029_m01_006: <ACA>Many of them were participants in the\nHeroic Games.
MID_EV13_029_m01_007: <ACA>I come with a warning from the temples to all the\nmost prominent clans in the games.
MID_EV13_029_m01_008: <ACA>Yet I also come seeking help resolving the matter.
MID_EV13_029_m01_009: <ACB>What is it you are really asking?
MID_EV13_029_m01_010: <ACB>I have heard you were attacked last night and that\nyou fended him off with ease.
MID_EV13_029_m01_011: <ACB>That is why I hope you will help us,\nQueen Theodora.
MID_EV13_029_m01_012: If we fail to settle the situation—if the culprit\nremains at large—the temples will lose face.
MID_EV13_029_m01_013: If you will not speak plainly, allow me.
MID_EV13_029_m01_014: The killer is Bahr Vahn, who has escaped from\ncustody. He is after Drake's treasures.
MID_EV13_029_m01_015: That is why his victims have been participants in\nthe Heroic Games, I take it.
MID_EV13_029_m01_016: I... No! Our investigation is ongoing.
MID_EV13_029_m01_017: The temples have their own elite warriors in the\nform of the vulkans.
MID_EV13_029_m01_018: Do they not say a single vulkan knight is a match\nfor a thousand soldiers?
MID_EV13_029_m01_019: Odd that you would seek aid from outsiders before\nmobilizing them.
MID_EV13_029_m01_020: Unless there is an element to this matter that\ncannot be made public.
MID_EV13_029_m01_021: Tch...
MID_EV13_029_m01_022: In truth, I care not. We cannot suffer this maniac\nto live either.
MID_EV13_029_m01_023: He is due soon to strike at me again.
MID_EV13_029_m01_024: How can you be so certain?
MID_EV13_029_m01_025: I understand him better than you might think.\nHe and I share a common ancestry.
MID_EV13_029_m01_026: Is this true?
MID_EV13_029_m01_027: The safest course would be to establish a curfew\nfor your citizens.
MID_EV13_029_m01_028: We will hunt the beast by night. You may join us\nif you have the stomach for it.
MID_EV13_030_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_030_m01_001: The White-Maned Demon lives up to his reputation.
MID_EV13_030_m01_002: To see him fight is a marvel. I feel as though it has\nlit a fire within me.
MID_EV13_030_m01_003: His opponent's technique was interesting as well.
MID_EV13_030_m01_004: It's not one I've seen often. Some form of spirit\ncasting, I would guess.
MID_EV13_030_m01_005: While we're on the subject of the White-Maned\nDemon, I learned something intriguing.
MID_EV13_030_m01_006: His true name is Bertrand. He was once a general\nin the kingdom of Arago.
MID_EV13_030_m01_007: His talent there afforded him a promising future.\nEven the princess of Arago took interest in him.
MID_EV13_030_m01_008: But then he was arrested for assassinating the king\nshortly after that business in Cydonia.
MID_EV13_030_m01_009: Just before his execution, the Divine Sovereign\ndecreed he would undergo the Trial of the Chariot.
MID_EV13_030_m01_010: A general of Arago, is he? I was certain he hailed\nfrom the kingdom of Brezarant.
MID_EV13_030_m01_011: Most believe that his regicide was spurred by the\nking's refusal to allow him to marry the princess.
MID_EV13_030_m01_012: That is the motivation one hears in fairy stories.\nI smell a conspiracy beneath it.
MID_EV13_030_m01_013: Do people truly believe that, or are they holding their\ntongues out of fear?
MID_EV13_030_m01_014: Any conspiracy would mean that one of the most\npowerful people in Arago was pulling the strings.
MID_EV13_030_m01_015: What is this "Trial of the Chariot" the man was\nsentenced to?
MID_EV13_030_m01_016: Ah, that. There's only one way for him to prove his\ninnocence and win his freedom.
MID_EV13_030_m01_017: Bertrand must cover the chariot of Mars, the Bringer\nof War, with gold earned in battle.
MID_EV13_030_m01_018: Over the past five years, the White-Maned Demon\nhas so far won nearly one thousand battles.
MID_EV13_030_m01_019: Impressive. I would love to recruit the man for my\nown entourage.
MID_EV13_030_m01_020: Is there not risk in that? If the rumors of his ambition\nare true, that is.
MID_EV13_030_m01_021: Perhaps I ought to cross blades with him sometime\nto get his measure for myself.
MID_EV13_031_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_031_m01_001: He stayed on his feet even after he lost\nconsciousness. The man's not lacking for will.
MID_EV13_031_m01_002: What a wonderful bout, you two! I am pleased to\nhave had such exclusive access to the match.
MID_EV13_031_m01_003: And Yanjin is still breathing? Very good.
MID_EV13_031_m01_004: The child is one of my favorite playthings.\nI'm grateful you didn't break him completely.
MID_EV13_031_m01_005: But the time has come for me to collect my damaged\ntoy and take him in for repairs.
MID_EV13_031_m01_006: You've done well, Bertrand. You, too, may\nreturn now.
MID_EV13_031_m01_007: Not just yet, if you please.
MID_EV13_031_m01_008: Lady of Lilies, I thank you for allowing me the\npleasure of an evening's entertainment.
MID_EV13_031_m01_009: I would test my own strength against this man.\nWould you mind if we crossed blades?
MID_EV13_031_m01_010: But of course. So long as he is amenable.
MID_EV13_031_m01_011: I am, yes—if there's money in it.
MID_EV13_031_m01_012: There is hardly a more suitable opponent for the\nWhite-Maned Demon than you, Queen Theodora.
MID_EV13_031_m01_013: Very well. I'll open my purse strings and pay a\ngenerous sum to the winner.
MID_EV13_031_m01_014: Your bearing is all that I hoped for.
MID_EV13_031_m01_015: I am Theodora Sergio Savangren, queen of the\nkingdom of Saramis.
MID_EV13_031_m01_016: We at last have time for a conversation. Come, let\nus not waste it.
MID_EV13_031_m01_017: Not with words, as nobles would, but as warriors—\nlet us speak with our blades.
MID_EV13_031_m01_018: Very well. Your move.
MID_EV13_031_m01_019: Hahaha. Show me the passion that has taken you\nthis far, White-Maned Demon!
MID_EV13_032_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_032_m01_001: Wait! Enough. I am satisfied.
MID_EV13_032_m01_002: What do you mean?
MID_EV13_032_m01_003: Was I not clear? I accept defeat. This victory\nis yours.
MID_EV13_032_m01_004: I see. Thank you.
MID_EV13_032_m01_005: A lovely match, you two. I will send the prize money\nto Gabriel.
MID_EV13_032_m01_006: Add 10 thousand gold of my own. It is money earned\nin battle, so I shall assume it counts.
MID_EV13_032_m01_007: Know that this is not a debt you are incurring.\nIt is a fair price for a thrilling match.
MID_EV13_032_m01_008: My time here has been unpleasant, to say the least.\nThis was a welcome change. Thank you.
MID_EV13_032_m01_009: Hehehe! I count myself lucky to have had a private\nview of such a thrilling match.
MID_EV13_032_m01_010: White-Maned Demon. Might I occupy a little more\nof your time?
MID_EV13_032_m01_011: I hear tell that you have won close to one thousand\nvictories thus far.
MID_EV13_032_m01_012: It is a magnificent streak against many of Dagda's\nmost skilled gladiators.
MID_EV13_032_m01_013: Well, I can't take all the credit. I have talented allies.
MID_EV13_032_m01_014: Do not be modest. That you have gathered such\nsteadfast allies is another of your strengths.
MID_EV13_032_m01_015: What would you say to entering my service?
MID_EV13_032_m01_016: I would never let a great warrior such as you toil\nin obscurity as you do now.
MID_EV13_032_m01_017: Oh, a great warrior? You mean the man they\ncharged with regicide?
MID_EV13_032_m01_018: It suggests a certain amount of arrogance, coming\nhere trusting that you wouldn't be killed.
MID_EV13_032_m01_019: I am in no danger. Your innocence became plain to\nme this evening.
MID_EV13_032_m01_020: What? How?
MID_EV13_032_m01_021: We spoke through combat. Your arguments\nwere sound.
MID_EV13_032_m01_022: You fight smoothly, as a pure warrior. One of low\nmoral character could never be so poetic.
MID_EV13_032_m01_023: I think it more likely that you have been made a\npawn in someone else's game.
MID_EV13_032_m01_024: Huh?
MID_EV13_032_m01_025: I put that belief to the test through combat, and you\nhave confirmed it to the hilt.
MID_EV13_032_m01_026: The day is not far off when your strength will prove\nyour innocence. Then you will be free.
MID_EV13_032_m01_027: When you are, come to me. Saramis has its own\nelite warriors, and they are fearsome, it is true.
MID_EV13_032_m01_028: But they are far from sufficient to defeat the Mosa,\nour longtime rivals—or an enemy even worse.
MID_EV13_032_m01_029: Worse than the Mosa?
MID_EV13_032_m01_030: I have said too much. If you know my people's\nhistory, you might guess at it. One must be prepared.
MID_EV13_032_m01_031: Know that my offer is sincere, and think on it.
MID_EV13_032_m01_032: Before I leave, answer me this... Have you ever heard\na voice while swinging that axe?
MID_EV13_032_m01_033: A voice? What are you on about?
MID_EV13_032_m01_034: No? Good. But it may be best for all concerned if\nyou part ways with that axe.
MID_EV13_032_m01_035: You are strong enough not to need it. It is more likely\nto be your downfall than your salvation.
MID_EV13_032_m01_036: The axe is a memento of a bond I had previously\nthought lost.
MID_EV13_032_m01_037: For that reason, I must keep it close.
MID_EV13_032_m01_038: Then you and I are more alike than I knew. That is\nall for now.
MID_EV13_032_m01_039: Queen Theodora of Saramis...
MID_EV13_032_m01_040: Well done, Your Majesty. What an intense fight!
MID_EV13_032_m01_041: Yes...it's been a fine evening. I feel ready for a good\nnight's sleep for the first time in a while.
MID_EV13_033_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_033_m01_001: I'm sorry to arrive late.
MID_EV13_033_m01_002: No matter. He is not yet here. Is the moon out?
MID_EV13_033_m01_003: The skies are clear, without a cloud in sight.\nThe full moon seems...bigger somehow.
MID_EV13_033_m01_004: You think he will show his face tonight,\nYour Majesty?
MID_EV13_033_m01_005: I know it. The Har Hali would not fail to act beneath\nsuch a moon.
MID_EV13_033_m01_006: To your positions, everyone. We must make ready\nfor his attack.
MID_EV13_033_m01_007: Years ago, he slew my father. Tonight, he pays for\nhis crimes. Let us hunt the beast!
MID_EV13_033_m01_008: Rrgh... As I vowed, I will wrest my arm back\nfrom you.
MID_EV13_033_m01_009: Hah! A Har Hali to the core. I knew you could not\nresist a strike by the full moon's light.
MID_EV13_033_m01_010: Hrah-HAH!
MID_EV13_033_m01_011: Simpleton. Did you think I failed to plan for\nyour arrival?
MID_EV13_033_m01_012: Fire!
MID_EV13_033_m01_013: Oof... Augh...
MID_EV13_033_m01_014: Did that do it? He's not getting away from me\nthis time!
MID_EV13_033_m01_015: Think me a coward if you like, but those without\nhonor deserve no more than this.
MID_EV13_033_m01_016: You are no longer a warrior. You are a mere beast\nstarved for power.
MID_EV13_033_m01_017: Tonight, I avenge my father at last!
MID_EV13_033_m01_018: Blugghh...
MID_EV13_033_m01_019: Oh no...was that flamma?!
MID_EV13_033_m01_020: Rrr... Rrr!
MID_EV13_033_m01_021: RAAAGH!
MID_EV13_033_m01_022: So the brute refuses to die. But he won't escape me\nagain. Everyone, follow me!
MID_EV13_034_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_034_m01_001: Queen Theodora, you have my thanks for your help\nresolving this incident.
MID_EV13_034_m01_002: Think nothing of it. The thorn in my side needed\nremoving anyway.
MID_EV13_034_m01_003: There'll be no miraculous resurrection for him now.\nNot after that.
MID_EV13_034_m01_004: You can trust us to take responsibility for disposing\nof the body.
MID_EV13_034_m01_005: <NCA>Express your doubts.
MID_EV13_034_m01_006: <NCB>Press Hong Hua.
MID_EV13_034_m01_007: <ACA>I wonder about that.
MID_EV13_034_m01_008: <ACA>During my bout with him and again just now, this\nman drank an elixir you called flamma.
MID_EV13_034_m01_009: <ACA>Might your faction be the ones who supplied it?
MID_EV13_034_m01_010: <ACA>You have been feigning ignorance. But you knew of\nthis man from the start.
MID_EV13_034_m01_011: <ACB>It was your faction who let this man slip free,\nwas it not?
MID_EV13_034_m01_012: I take it you belong to the Order of Mithras.
MID_EV13_034_m01_013: Ah!
MID_EV13_034_m01_014: He told me to "return" this arm of mine, an arm\nthat some have called one of Drake's treasures.
MID_EV13_034_m01_015: What are Drake's treasures, truly? I would have you\ntell me all you know.
MID_EV13_034_m01_016: They're...remains. Of a certain exalted person.
MID_EV13_034_m01_017: What?! Explain yourself.
MID_EV13_034_m01_018: I've said as much as I can. But even as a corpse,\nthey held unearthly power.
MID_EV13_034_m01_019: When broken into pieces and scattered across Dagda,\nthey came to be called Drake's treasures.
MID_EV13_034_m01_020: Our organization has been tasked with their\nswift recovery.
MID_EV13_034_m01_021: Your arm is one of them, Queen Theodora.
MID_EV13_034_m01_022: As I feared...it never came from a spirit of the land.
MID_EV13_034_m01_023: But how did Mahadu come by it?
MID_EV13_034_m01_024: One question more. In time, will I share that\nman's fate?
MID_EV13_034_m01_025: It's...hard to say. From what I understand, it varies\ngreatly depending on the bearer.
MID_EV13_034_m01_026: I respect you, Queen Theodora. And I wish I had\nleave to say more. Alas...
MID_EV13_034_m01_027: I sincerely pray for your safety and that the dream\nwhich led you here is fulfilled.
MID_EV13_034_m01_028: Is the audience over, Your Majesty?
MID_EV13_034_m01_029: Yes. It has been a long time coming, but I have\nfinally avenged Father.
MID_EV13_034_m01_030: Kill them all...
MID_EV13_034_m01_031: Bonaventure? Did you say something?
MID_EV13_034_m01_032: Huh? No, Your Majesty.
MID_EV13_034_m01_033: I see. It has been a taxing night. Please leave me\nbe for a while.
MID_EV13_034_m01_034: Ah?
MID_EV13_034_m01_035: Troy's amulet? The warding chain has shattered.
MID_EV13_034_m01_036: Is my time short? Will I be no better than that\nmonster soon?
MID_EV13_035_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_035_m01_001: With the help of Queen Theodora of Saramis, I have\nrecovered Bahr Vahn.
MID_EV13_035_m01_002: Good work. He certainly made himself a nuisance.
MID_EV13_035_m01_003: Speaking of the queen of Saramis, she is descended\nfrom the Dagsion prisoners, yes?
MID_EV13_035_m01_004: Were you interested in her for her connection to your\nhomeland, or did she remind you of your lost child?
MID_EV13_035_m01_005: Not that it matters.
MID_EV13_035_m01_006: You should continue to cultivate Theodora's trust.\nShe is a useful pawn.
MID_EV13_035_m01_007: It will be done as you say.
MID_EV13_035_m01_008: Raksha? I've extracted the remains from our man.
MID_EV13_035_m01_009: That Bahr Vahn managed to surprise me.
MID_EV13_035_m01_010: He was still breathing as we removed the treasures,\neven as his body was in tatters.
MID_EV13_035_m01_011: Such astounding resilience... It's hard to believe he\nwas human. Maybe the remains made him that way.
MID_EV13_035_m01_012: Hehehe! Oh well. We put him in the device and\nturned him into flamma. That's the end of that!
MID_EV13_035_m01_013: He believed himself to be Father until the very end,\nyou know.
MID_EV13_035_m01_014: Yes. Bearers of Drake's treasures are inevitably\novertaken by his residual consciousness.
MID_EV13_035_m01_015: That is the will of our father, who detested this land\nand attempted to slaughter all who dwelled in it.
MID_EV13_035_m01_016: Ultimately, the self is lost. They fully become soldiers\nof the underworld, capable only of obeying that will.
MID_EV13_035_m01_017: Though tolerances vary, normal humans cannot\nwithstand it. They always succumb in the end.
MID_EV13_035_m01_018: That is why many who possess Drake's treasures end\ntheir lives early.
MID_EV13_035_m01_019: Unless, like us, they are of Father's direct bloodline.
MID_EV13_035_m01_020: Sounds like Bahr Vahn was a special boy.
MID_EV13_035_m01_021: But not so special that he could hold on to himself.\nWhat a disappointment.
MID_EV13_035_m01_022: How will you fare, Queen Theodora?